x86_64-linux  clang emits only the C2 variant of a constructor it writes for a class, where cxx1 emits C1 and C2 as it does for all of them - so cxx1's set has _ZN6HolderC1Ev in it and clang's does not. Nothing here is about arrays: Holder declares no constructor, so the one that builds its `S a[2]` member is written by the compiler and is inline by nature with no out-of-line form to switch to, which is the same difference implicit-move.nonames and move-constructor.nonames already record. C1 and C2 are identical for a class with no virtual bases and both are mergeable definitions, so the extra C1 costs object size and nothing else. arm64-darwin emits both and agrees on all 7 names, and x86_64-windows agrees on all 4.
